{
    "background_story": "Ada was a young Nepali artist who grew up in the vibrant streets of Kathmandu. She was fascinated by the rich cultural heritage of her country and spent most of her childhood learning traditional Nepali dances and music. As she grew older, Ada became increasingly interested in preserving the traditional crafts of Nepal, particularly the ancient art of thangka painting. She spent years honing her skills under the guidance of a local master artist and soon became known for her exquisite paintings that blended traditional techniques with modern themes. Ada's art gained international recognition, and she was invited to showcase her work in galleries around the world. Through her art, Ada aimed to share the beauty and diversity of Nepali culture with the world, while also supporting local artisans and preserving the country's rich heritage.",
